                    "title": "Bài 1 · Introduction to Circuit Protection",
                    "instruction": "Read the text and answer the questions.",
                    "instruction_vi": "",
                    "passage": "Circuit protection devices are fundamental components in electrical engineering. They prevent catastrophic fires and equipment damage caused by overcurrent or short circuits.\n\nA fuse contains a thin wire designed to melt when the current exceeds a specific threshold. Once blown, a fuse must be replaced manually. In contrast, a circuit breaker uses an electromagnetic or thermal switch that trips automatically when excessive current flows. Circuit breakers can be reset after the fault is cleared, making them far more convenient for modern residential and industrial installations.",
                    "config": {},
                    "questions": [
